  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/bd478e9925303e3d018e2d070e4e3a78e72fb699a48ac3109ddf743158bb5599.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =P(Z<0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =\u03a6(0.38)-\u03a6(-0.19)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-0.38) & =0.3520 \\\\ \u03a6(-0.19) & =0.4247,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $\u03a6(0.38).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(0.38) & =P(Z\\le 0.38) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.38) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(-0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.3520 \\\\  & =0.6480\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =\u03a6(0.38)-\u03a6(-0.19) \\\\  & =0.6480-0.4247 \\\\  & =0.2233.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
